# pstack on this project

This repo is Daniel A Rodrigues's static portfolio. One shared content source drives the scrollable site and the project case studies. Skills live in `.cursor/skills/`. Agents live in `.cursor/agents/`. Read a skill before you follow it.

## Always

- Apply `unslop` to every reply and any prose you write.
- Name the data shape first (`principle-model-the-domain`). Project origin is `"work" | "personal"`, not an optional bag.
- Smallest change that solves it (`principle-laziness-protocol`).
- Prove UI in the running app, not only that it compiles (`principle-prove-it-works`). Home and `/projects/:slug` share content modules. Check the surfaces that read what you changed. Asset URLs must use `publicUrl()` because GitHub Pages serves under `/portfolio-fe/`.
- TypeScript edits follow `typescript-best-practices`.
- No narrating comments. Keep a comment only for a non-obvious why the code cannot show (`no-comments`).
- Editorial feel beats implementation convenience (`principle-experience-first`): `surface-*` / `glow` tokens, serif headings, no card wrappers, no `zinc-*` or raw hex.

## Invariants from this repo

- Portfolio facts live in `@src/shared/profile.ts` and `@src/shared/projects.ts`. Update those first when bio, jobs, or projects change.
- `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts` interpolates those modules. Keep it compiling. Do not import it from the Vite client.
- There is no chat overlay, no command registry, and no API client.
- Browser public files go through `@src/lib/publicUrl.ts`. Do not hardcode `/resume.pdf` or `/profile.png`.
- Unit tests go under `tests/` mirroring `src/`. Never hit live APIs.
- After a large feature, layout change, or contract change, update `.cursor/rules/` in the same PR (`sync-cursor-rules`).

## Task routing

- Non-trivial feature, bug, refactor, or prototype: read `poteto-mode` and copy the matching playbook steps in verbatim.
- Types or calls that cross a function boundary: `architect` first.
- "How does X work": `how`.
- "Why is this this way": `why`.
- Small-looking change: `blast-radius` before editing. Experience timeline and project routes share `projects.ts`.
- Bug with a cheap local test: `tdd`.
- Docs, commits, PR descriptions: `technical-writing`. Keep PR bodies short using `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.
- No playbook fits, or the user is stepping away: `figure-it-out`.
- `.cursor/skills/verify-*` is missing: `create-verification-skill` (browser drive of the Vite app).

## Do not load

`make-bot-ui`, `automate-me`, `setup-pstack`, and `bro` are not part of this project.

## Do not reintroduce

Telegram notify, title-generation endpoints, album/music theme switching, a global footer with duplicate contact links, an inline hero terminal, a sidebar chat panel, a terminal command registry, `import { … } from 'simple-icons'`, the FastAPI `mira_project` backend, Next.js App Router, or a live OpenRouter/Mongo chat stack unless explicitly requested.
